&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Anthropic&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Anthropic’s mission is to create reliable, interpretable, and steerable AI systems. We want AI to be safe and beneficial for our users and for society as a whole. Our team is a quickly growing group of committed researchers, engineers, policy experts, and business leaders working together to build beneficial AI systems.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;About the role&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Communications Manager at Anthropic, you will bring The Anthropic Institute&#39;s research to the world. The Institute works to advance the public conversation around AI, publishing findings so that policymakers, researchers, journalists, and the public can reckon with what&#39;s here and prepare for what&#39;s ahead.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will provide dedicated communications coverage for the Institute&#39;s two largest and fastest growing research engines: 1) Economic Research, which tracks AI&#39;s effect on jobs, wages, and the broader economy through the Anthropic Economic Index and labor market analysis, and 2) Societal Impacts, which studies how Claude is actually used, from workplace impacts and personal guidance to Claude&#39;s values and frontier agent use. You’ll also support TAI’s other teams, including Special Projects and the Frontier Red Team.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In this role, you&#39;ll drive research tracking, publication strategy, and reactive press across both portfolios, including launches like quarterly Economic Index releases and the rollout of the new Economic Research Fund. You&#39;ll partner closely with the Economic Research and Societal Impacts research teams day to day, work alongside the Deputy Communications Lead, and coordinate with Anthropic&#39;s broader communications, policy, and editorial teams to keep messaging aligned while maintaining the Institute&#39;s distinct voice.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive day-to-day communications for the Economic Research and Societal Impacts teams, including research tracking, publication planning, and reactive press&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead communications planning and launch execution for the Anthropic Economic Index, recurring labor market analyses, and new research initiatives like the Economic Research Fund&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop narratives that translate technical and quantitative research for audiences well beyond specialist communities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and maintain relationships with reporters across economics, labor, technology, research, and general interest outlets, along with academic economists and think tank researchers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Draft communications plans, briefing documents, talking points, press materials, and social content&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage reactive press on sensitive findings in partnership with the Communications Lead, Deputy Communications Lead, and policy team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with policy and editorial teams on publishing strategy, ensuring research reaches the largest appropriate audience through the Anthropic blog, the Institute&#39;s site, microsites, interactive experiences, video, and audio&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Present researchers for media interviews, podcast appearances, and speaking engagements, and prepare them to succeed in those moments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Institute communications leadership on major announcements and milestone engagements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build repeatable rollout playbooks and processes that allow a lean team to cover a growing research portfolio&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track both teams&#39; research agendas to shape findings early and plan publications months in advance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;You may be a good fit if you&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have deep communications experience, with significant depth in research, science, economics, or policy communications&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have a track record of translating complex, technical, or academic research into public narratives that reach audiences well beyond specialist communities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Are comfortable reading and interrogating quantitative research, and can engage substantively and credibly with the researchers who produce it&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have strong, active media relationships&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Can move between long-lead strategic messaging and fast-turnaround tactical execution without losing quality, from planning a launch months out to handling an inbound press inquiry the same day&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have led multi-channel rollouts spanning strategy, digital, press, and cross-functional approvals&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Are intellectually curious about AI&#39;s impact on the economy, society, and the future of work, and can embrace the unexpected in a field where the unusual is the norm&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Thrive in fast-moving environments where priorities shift and ambiguity is common&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Are excited about Anthropic&#39;s mission to develop AI that is safe and beneficial&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Strong candidates may also have&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience at a research institution, think tank, economics publication, or policy organization communicating quantitative findings&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with the AI policy landscape and the debates around AI&#39;s labor market and societal impacts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience standing up communications processes or playbooks on a small, growing team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A background working directly with economists, social scientists, or academic researchers on publication strategy&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing sensitive or high-scrutiny press moments, including deciding what to say, when, and how&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Enthusiasm for using AI tools in your own workflows to multiply what a small team can do&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;The annual compensation range for this role is listed below.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;For sales roles, the range provided is the role’s On Target Earnings (&quot;OTE&quot;) range, meaning that the range includes both the sales commissions/sales bonuses target and annual base salary for the role.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Annual Salary:&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$265,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$295,000 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Logistics&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum education: &lt;/strong&gt;Bachelor’s degree or an equivalent combination of education, training, and/or experience&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required field of study:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;A field relevant to the role as demonstrated through coursework, training, or professional experience&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum years of experience: &lt;/strong&gt;Years of experience required will correlate with the internal job level requirements for the position&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location-based hybrid policy:&lt;/strong&gt; Currently, we expect all staff to be in one of our offices at least 25% of the time. However, some roles may require more time in our offices.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong data-stringify-type=&quot;bold&quot;&gt;Visa sponsorship:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;We do sponsor visas! However, we aren&#39;t able to successfully sponsor visas for every role and every candidate. But if we make you an offer, we will make every reasonable effort to get you a visa, and we retain an immigration lawyer to help with this.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We encourage you to apply even if you do not believe you meet every single qualification.&lt;/strong&gt; Not all strong candidates will meet every single qualification as listed.&amp;nbsp; Research shows that people who identify as being from underrepresented groups are more prone to experiencing imposter syndrome and doubting the strength of their candidacy, so we urge you not to exclude yourself prematurely and to submit an application if you&#39;re interested in this work. We think AI systems like the ones we&#39;re building have enormous social and ethical implications. We think this makes representation even more important, and we strive to include a range of diverse perspectives on our team.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong data-stringify-type=&quot;bold&quot;&gt;Your safety matters to us.&lt;/strong&gt; To protect yourself from potential scams, remember that Anthropic recruiters only contact you from&amp;nbsp;@anthropic.com&amp;nbsp;email addresses. In some cases, we may partner with vetted recruiting agencies who will identify themselves as working on behalf of Anthropic. Be cautious of emails from other domains. Legitimate Anthropic recruiters will never ask for money, fees, or banking information before your first day. If you&#39;re ever unsure about a communication, don&#39;t click any links—visit&amp;nbsp;&lt;u data-stringify-type=&quot;underline&quot;&gt;&lt;a class=&quot;c-link c-link--underline&quot; href=&quot;http://anthropic.com/careers&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; data-stringify-link=&quot;http://anthropic.com/careers&quot; data-sk=&quot;tooltip_parent&quot; data-remove-tab-index=&quot;true&quot;&gt;anthropic.com/careers&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/u&gt;&amp;nbsp;directly for confirmed position openings.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;How we&#39;re different&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We believe that the highest-impact AI research will be big science. At Anthropic we work as a single cohesive team on just a few large-scale research efforts. And we value impact — advancing our long-term goals of steerable, trustworthy AI — rather than work on smaller and more specific puzzles. We view AI research as an empirical science, which has as much in common with physics and biology as with traditional efforts in computer science. We&#39;re an extremely collaborative group, and we host frequent research discussions to ensure that we are pursuing the highest-impact work at any given time. As such, we greatly value communication skills.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The easiest way to understand our research directions is to read our recent research. This research continues many of the directions our team worked on prior to Anthropic, including: GPT-3, Circuit-Based Interpretability, Multimodal Neurons, Scaling Laws, AI &amp;amp; Compute, Concrete Problems in AI Safety, and Learning from Human Preferences.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Come work with us!&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Anthropic is a public benefit corporation headquartered in San Francisco. We offer competitive compensation and benefits, optional equity donation matching, generous vacation and parental leave, flexible working hours, and a lovely office space in which to collaborate with colleagues. &lt;strong data-stringify-type=&quot;bold&quot;&gt;Guidance on Candidates&#39; AI Usage:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;Learn about&amp;nbsp;&lt;a class=&quot;c-link&quot; href=&quot;https://www.anthropic.com/candidate-ai-guidance&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; data-stringify-link=&quot;https://www.anthropic.com/candidate-ai-guidance&quot; data-sk=&quot;tooltip_parent&quot;&gt;our policy&lt;/a&gt; for using AI in our application process.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Anthropic&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Anthropic’s mission is to create reliable, interpretable, and steerable AI systems. We want AI to be safe and beneficial for our users and for society as a whole. Our team is a quickly growing group of committed researchers, engineers, policy experts, and business leaders working together to build beneficial AI systems.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;About the role&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Anthropic&#39;s Life Sciences team is building a research group focused on biological discoveries by combining AI with hands-on biological research. We&#39;re seeking a research scientist who combines deep chemistry knowledge with machine learning expertise to join the team. Our goal is to speed up progress in the life sciences by an order of magnitude, and this role puts that mission into practice. You&#39;ll be a computational chemist who knows reactions, synthesis, and medicinal chemistry in depth and has hands-on experience training and evaluating machine learning models. Above all, you&#39;ll build the reinforcement learning environments, datasets, and evaluations that teach Claude chemistry. Working alongside our bench chemists and AI researchers, you&#39;ll turn real chemistry problems and experimental data into training tasks and measure whether the models get better at them.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role is fully on-site in the San Francisco Bay Area.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Key responsibilities&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and build reinforcement learning environments for chemistry end to end, including task design, data curation, automated grading, and checks against shortcuts and data leakage&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and source new experimental datasets, environments, and evaluations with our bench chemists, and external research and academic partners&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop evaluations that measure model performance on real chemistry tasks, such as reaction outcome prediction, synthesis planning, structure elucidation, and compound design, and feed results back to research teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Run and analyze training experiments with AI research teams, diagnose where models fail at chemistry, and prioritize what to build next&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure datasets and environments are high quality and well documented, including sources, train and test splits, and failure modes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Communicate findings clearly to chemistry, AI research, and life sciences audiences&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Minimum qualifications&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;PhD in chemistry, computational chemistry, or a related field&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep knowledge of organic and medicinal chemistry, including reactions, synthesis, and SAR, with experimental data as your ground truth&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong Python skills and solid machine learning fundamentals, with hands-on experience training and evaluating models&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort navigating ambiguity and defining problems in a rapidly evolving research environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work independently while collaborating effectively across cross-functional teams, with strong written and verbal communication skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with reinforcement learning, large language models, or building evaluations and benchmarks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track record of supporting drug discovery programs alongside medicinal and synthetic chemists&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience curating chemistry datasets from the literature, patents, or lab notebooks, including reaction, ADMET, and spectroscopic data&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Cheminformatics and molecular modeling skills, for example RDKit, docking, free energy calculations, or quantum chemistry&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on synthetic or medicinal chemistry experience at the bench&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Publications, patents, or open-source software demonstrating scientific impact&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;The annual compensation range for this role is listed below.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
